Description: Fix protoc-gen-js libc++ runtime linking
 protoc-gen-js uses std::__Cr:: symbols but doesn't explicitly depend on libc++.
 With use_custom_libcxx=true, the link command includes -nostdlib++ but doesn't
 link libc++.a, causing undefined symbol errors at task 1600/76623.
 .
 This patch adds an explicit dependency on //buildtools/third_party/libc++ to
 ensure proper linking of the bundled libc++ static library.
 .
 Error: ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: std::__Cr::__libcpp_verbose_abort
        ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: operator new(unsigned long)
        ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: operator delete(void*)
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-11-10

diff --git a/third_party/protobuf-javascript/BUILD.gn b/third_party/protobuf-javascript/BUILD.gn
index 0000000000..1111111111 100644
--- a/third_party/protobuf-javascript/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/protobuf-javascript/BUILD.gn
@@ -16,6 +16,10 @@ if (current_toolchain == host_toolchain) {
     deps = [
       "//third_party/protobuf:protoc_lib",

+      # Debian: Explicitly depend on libc++ for proper linking with use_custom_libcxx=true
+      "//buildtools/third_party/libc++",
+      "//buildtools/third_party/libc++abi",
+
       # Default manifest on Windows (a no-op elsewhere).
       "//build/win:default_exe_manifest",
     ]
